WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.902
-We are back with
Daniel Craig, everyone.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.237
One question on a lot of
people's minds is,

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.571
"Who is the next Bond?"

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:07.840
And I know that you're
not involved or maybe you are,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:13.112
but what advice would you give
to the next Bond?

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.547
-Don't [bleep] it up.
I mean...

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:18.051
-[ Laughs ] Oh, my God.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.852
Oh, my gosh. That is genius.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:22.655
-It's a beautiful, beautiful,
amazing thing.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:26.058
It's like, don't [bleep] it up.

00:00:26.058 --> 00:00:27.860
Leave it better
than when you found it.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.194
-That's great.

00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:32.598
-Is that right? Can I say that?
Probably not. Okay.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:33.800
-You are allowed to do
whatever you want.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.101
You're James Bond. Come on.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:38.638
You cannot have a Bond movie
without a great song.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.873
And you have
a great one in this.

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:45.445
Billie Eilish and Finneas wrote
and recorded "No Time to Die."

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.614
They're going to perform it,
actually, tonight on our show.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.048
-I'm so excited to see that.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.183
-How do you hear the songs when
they send it to you?

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:54.621
Do they go,
"Okay, what do you think?

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.456
-Well, what normally
happens is that

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.858
there's a sort of
rough cut of the song

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.860
that the musician will record.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.096
And it happened with Adele

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.531
and it happened
with Billie, as well.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:10.670
And it's sort of secretly sent
on a music file to a phone,

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.806
and we all kind of keep it --
You know, we try and keep it

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:15.074
as secret as we possibly can,

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.143
because it's important
to keep it under wraps.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.445
But I kind of want to -- I need
to listen to it.

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:21.714
And earphones
are never quite good enough,

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:25.118
and my office at Pinewood
is next to other offices,

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.319
so I can't crank it up.

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:30.790
So, there's usually
a fancy car parked outside

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.393
somewhere at Pinewood,
whether it's an Aston Martin

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.027
or it's a Range Rover
or something,

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:37.930
and they tend to have
pretty good stereos in them.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.432
So I'll get in the car
and drive it somewhere

00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:42.301
and then just crank it up

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:45.104
and listen to it
like 10 or 15 times.

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:46.439
'Cause then you get it --

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.508
Because you need to kind of
vibrate with the song.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:52.578
And, you know, this song is --
Especially with Billie's song,

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.814
it was just like,
"Well, we've got this."

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.215
-If you had to pick your
three favorite

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:57.216
Bond songs of all time --

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:58.284
-Oh, no!

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.852
-No, but not including
"No Time to Die."

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:01.854
-Okay, okay, okay, okay.
-Not including "No Time to Die."

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.457
-Okay, you go first.
-Me go first?

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.625
-Yes.

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:10.463
-I think you got "Goldfinger,"
Shirley Bassey.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:11.998
♪ Goldfinger ♪

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.099
♪ He's the man ♪

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.568
I love that one. I love --
-It's great.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.470
Those horns are so violent.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.105
I listened to that
again recently.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:23.509
It's really, like, a scream.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:25.811
-I like "Thunderball,"
Tom Jones.

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:27.980
-Yeah. You know
the story of that one,

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.348
don't you, with Tom Jones?

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:30.783
-No.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.219
-Supposedly, on the last take,
which was the one they used,

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.622
he held the note for so long,
he passed out in the booth.

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:38.791
You ever hear that?
-No.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.459
-I don't know if it's true,
but I love it.

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:42.061
I like to think it's true.
-For that last...

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.764
♪ Thunderba-a-a-a-a-ll ♪

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:47.867
Oh, my gosh.
That's the only way to do it.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:50.202
-They were like, "Wow, Tom!
That's great, Tom."

00:02:50.202 --> 00:02:52.805
Where has he gone?"

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.641
-Yeah, I mean, honestly,
there's so many good ones.

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:58.110
I would say "Live and Let Die."

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.745
-Yeah, no, that's great.

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:02.615
I mean, truly, I'll leave
this one out the way,

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.150
but I think this is brilliant,
Billie's,

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.485
and it's definitely up there.

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:08.788
I mean, in fact,
it's in the top three.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.923
But if I have to name,
I mean, Adele is --

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:13.993 line:0%
When I first heard that,
that was like, "Oh, my God."

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:18.163 line:0%
I've got a sort of soft spot for
"GoldenEye" because of Tina.

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:19.532 line:0%
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:23.870
-And "Nobody Does It Better,"
because it's so kind of

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.272
not a Bond theme,
but it's Carly Simon,

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:29.309
and I had a
massive, massive, massive crush

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.243
on Carly Simon when I was a kid.

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:33.412
-We have something
very special tonight.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:36.482
You brought an exclusive clip
from "No Time to Die"

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.684
that we are premiering tonight.

00:03:38.684 --> 00:03:42.321
Before we show it, is there
any setup you want to give or --

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:44.757
-I think this is
the one which comes towards

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.593
the beginning of the movie,
where, you know,

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:49.796
when I read the script
and it says,

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:54.434
"Run down bridge
and be chased by the bad guys,

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:58.004
jump off bridge,"
it's like, "Oh, here we go."

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.272
-Here we go.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:02.241
Here's Daniel Craig in
"No Time to Die."

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:03.476
Take a look.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:06.512
♪♪

00:04:16.455 --> 00:04:18.758
[ Bullets ricocheting,
tires screech ]

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:53.759
-Yes! Come on! Standing ovation!
Oh, my gosh!

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:56.495
Yes! Yes!
That's what we want.

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:58.897
I love it.
Daniel Craig, you are awesome.

00:04:58.897 --> 00:05:01.534
"No Time to Die"
hits theaters in the spring.

